Porsche AG is a renowned German automobile manufacturer specializing in luxury, high-performance sports cars, SUVs, and sedans. The company is a subsidiary of Volkswagen AG, which in turn is majority-owned by the holding company Porsche Automobil Holding SE. 
What Porsche Does
Porsche designs, manufactures, and sells premium vehicles, engines, and parts, and provides financial and engineering services. The company is synonymous with performance, prestige, and German engineering heritage. 
Key business areas include:
Vehicle Manufacturing and Sales: The core business involves the development, production, and global sale of its distinctive model lineup through a network of over 900 dealerships.
Financial Services: This segment offers customer and dealer financing, leasing, service, and insurance brokerage for Porsche vehicles, and occasionally for other Volkswagen Group brands like Bentley and Lamborghini.
Engineering Services: Porsche Engineering provides consulting and development work for vehicles and engines, including data processing solutions and the commercial exploitation of intellectual property rights.
Motorsport: Porsche has a rich history in racing and uses the cutting edge of motorsport (e.g., Formula E) to develop innovative, sustainable technologies for its road cars. 
Products and Services Sold
Porsche offers a focused portfolio of six core passenger car models, with increasing investment in electrification. 
911: The iconic, rear-engine sports car with 2 doors and 2+2 seats.
718 Boxster and Cayman: Precise, mid-engine sports cars for pure driving pleasure.
Taycan: Porsche's first series production battery-electric vehicle model, offering a pure electric sports car experience.
Panamera: A luxury sedan with a high level of comfort.
Macan: A sporty compact SUV, now also available as a new all-electric model.
Cayenne: A versatile, full-size SUV that can seat up to five, with hybrid and gasoline options. 
In addition to standard models, Porsche offers:
Porsche Exclusive Manufaktur: A bespoke personalization program that allows customers to individualize their vehicles with unique designs and features.
Porsche Sonderwunsch: A "special request" program for building customers' unique dream cars. 
Corporate Governance and Board Members
Porsche AG is a public limited company (Aktiengesellschaft or AG), but it is largely controlled by the Porsche and Piëch families through a complex ownership structure involving Volkswagen AG and Porsche Automobil Holding SE. 
Executive Board (Vorstand)
The Executive Board manages the day-to-day business of Porsche AG. 
Dr. Michael Leiters: Chief Executive Officer (effective Jan 1, 2026).
Dr. Jochen Breckner: Member of the Executive Board – Finance and IT (effective Feb 26, 2025).
Matthias Becker: Member of the Executive Board – Sales and Marketing (effective Feb 26, 2025).
Dr. Michael Steiner: Deputy Chairman and Member of the Executive Board – Research and Development.
Sajjad Khan: Member of the Executive Board – Car-IT.
Albrecht Reimold: Member of the Executive Board – Production and Logistics.
Vera Schalwig: Member of the Executive Board – Human Resources.
Joachim Scharnagl: Member of the Executive Board – Procurement. 
Supervisory Board (Aufsichtsrat)
The Supervisory Board oversees the Executive Board.
Wolfgang Porsche: Chairman of the Supervisory Board.
